= The Progressives flailing

The Progressive Party of Saskatchewan, a coalition partner of Anderson's Cooperative Coalition faces a difficult headwind with the UFC(SS)'s decision to back a new Farmer-Labour Party rather than align with the existing parties. Itself a self-proclaimed voice for the farmers, it seems the PPS' days are numbered. 

There are various currents within the party. Some seek to join the Conservatives and continue managing the Depression. Others see the FLP as the reincarnation of original prairie revolt against the established parties. Still some seek to join the Liberals. 

As an established party, the PPS maintains riding organizations that we would otherwise have to set up ourselves. 

- @pps_merge: Can we merge with the Progressives? 
- @pps_cancel: The Progressives didn't get anywhere anyway

@pps_merge
subtitle: We would be incorporating non-socialists into the party

= PPS Negotations

The PPS is concerned about our socialist platform. We must make concessions to entice the party into a merger. 

- @remove_use_lease: Abandon Use-lease
- @abandon_socialism: Remove all mentions of Socialism from our platform
- @support_cooperative_coalition: Continue supporting the Cooperative Coalition
- @pps_cancel: The PPS asks too much of us

@remove_use_lease
